{"name":"Roasted Seeds","hex":"#e1a175","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"roasted","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cooked by roasting."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of roast"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roasted"},{"term":"seeds","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of seed"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of seed"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seeds"}],"entries":[{"title":"Roasting","blocks":[{"text":"Roasting is a cooking method that uses dry heat where hot air covers the food, cooking it evenly on all sides with temperatures of at least 150 °C (300 °F) from an open flame, oven, or other heat source. Roasting can enhance the flavor through caramelization and Maillard browning on the surface of the food. Roasting uses indirect, diffused heat, and is suitable for slower cooking of meat in a larger, whole piece. Meats and most root and bulb vegetables can be roasted. Any piece of meat, especially red meat, that has been cooked in this fashion is called a roast. Meats and vegetables prepared in this way are described as \"roasted\", e.g., roasted chicken or roasted squash."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Roast_Pig_1.JPG/330px-Roast_Pig_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roasting"},{"title":"Seed","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a seed is a plant structure containing an embryo and stored nutrients in a protective coat called a testa. More generally, the term seed means anything that can be sown, which may include seed and husk or tuber. Seeds are the product of the ripened ovule, after the embryo sac is fertilized by sperm from pollen, forming a zygote. The embryo within a seed develops from the zygote and grows within the mother plant to a certain size before growth is halted."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/%D0%A0%D0%B0%D0%B7%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%BE%D0%B1%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B7%D0%B8%D0%B5_%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BC%D1%8F%D0%BD.jpg/330px-%D0%A0%D0%B0%D0%B7%D0%BD%D0%BE%D0%BE%D0%B1%D1%80%D0%B0%D0%B7%D0%B8%D0%B5_%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BC%D1%8F%D0%BD.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seed"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Roasting_meat_at_Hampton_Court_Palace.JPG/500px-Roasting_meat_at_Hampton_Court_Palace.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Roasting_meat_at_Hampton_Court_Palace.JPG/1280px-Roasting_meat_at_Hampton_Court_Palace.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Roasting_meat_at_Hampton_Court_Palace.JPG/500px-Roasting_meat_at_Hampton_Court_Palace.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Tudor style roasting meat on a spit","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARoasting_meat_at_Hampton_Court_Palace.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Sunday_roast_-_roast_beef_1.jpg/500px-Sunday_roast_-_roast_beef_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Sunday_roast_-_roast_beef_1.jpg/500px-Sunday_roast_-_roast_beef_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Sunday roast consisting of roast beef, potatoes, vegetables, and Yorkshire pudding","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASunday_roast_-_roast_beef_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Max%27s_Roasted_Chicken_-_Evan_Swigart.jpg/500px-Max%27s_Roasted_Chicken_-_Evan_Swigart.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.